sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-36> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "A fair fraction of the unsolved problems seriously studied in number theory will turn out to be questions that cannot be answered using the standard axioms of arithmetic.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Many open number-theory problems may be unprovable from arithmetic's axioms";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 12, “The Principle of Computational Equivalence”; section “Implications for Mathematics and Its Foundations” (from p. 772), p. 791. Scope: open problems in number theory relative to Peano arithmetic"
}
